**New Evidence**
- Official annual-report speech establishing the 2022 governing program and claimed progress.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Discurso del presidente Andrés Manuel López Obrador en el Cuarto Informe de Gobierno","publisher":"Presidencia de la República 2018-2024 / Gobierno de México","publication_date":"2022-09-01","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/discurso-del-presidente-andres-manuel-lopez-obrador-en-el-cuarto-informe-de-gobierno/","claim":"AMLO framed the 2022 program as having restored the pre-COVID economy while advancing social programs, pensions, the Tren Maya, aduanas modernization, and other infrastructure, and he claimed these results showed the transformation project was working.","locator":"opening paragraphs and the passages on employment, income, Tren Maya, aduanas, and infrastructure","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary annual-report speech from the ruler; strong for declared program and claimed progress, weaker for independent proof of success.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO; it is his own account of priorities and progress, not independent verification.","contrary_evidence":["Independent sources still flagged weak investment, high inequality, and incomplete implementation in 2022."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.10"]}
- Austerity as operating method and resource-allocation strategy.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Austeridad es un asunto de principios, afirma presidente; Gobierno de México fomenta ahorros en beneficio de la gente","publisher":"Presidencia de la República 2018-2024 / Gobierno de México","publication_date":"2022-07-28","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/austeridad-es-un-asunto-de-principios-afirma-presidente-gobierno-de-mexico-fomenta-ahorros-en-beneficio-de-la-gente/","claim":"AMLO said austerity meant cutting nonessential spending, travel, and operating costs without firing workers so savings could be redirected to the people and strategic development projects.","locator":"conference transcript quoted in the article","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong evidence for what he said and how he framed the method; weaker as proof that the method improved effectiveness.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and tied to the year's operating method.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own stated approach; it supports program translation but not success by itself.","contrary_evidence":["Austerity claims do not by themselves show better execution, lower waste, or improved outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}
- Creation of a new health institution for uninsured populations.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DECRETO por el que se crea el organismo público descentralizado denominado Servicios de Salud del Instituto Mexicano del Seguro Social para el Bienestar (IMSS-BIENESTAR)","publisher":"Diario Oficial de la Federación / Presidencia de la República","publication_date":"2022-08-31","url":"https://www.dof.gob.mx/nota_detalle.php?codigo=5663064&fecha=31%2F08%2F2022","claim":"The decree created IMSS-BIENESTAR to extend free and progressively expanded health services to people without social security.","locator":"decree text and the constitutional-health justification in the opening recital","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Formal legal act in the target year; very strong for the existence and stated purpose of the institution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Direct executive action under AMLO; it shows ownership of the institutional change, though service quality and coverage gains require separate evidence.","contrary_evidence":["The decree alone does not prove effective rollout, quality, or durable coverage expansion in 2022."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.9"]}
- Concrete infrastructure commitment in 2022.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Presidente anuncia inversión de 10 mil mdp para obras de infraestructura en Cancún y Tulum","publisher":"Presidencia de la República 2018-2024 / Gobierno de México","publication_date":"2022-01-29","url":"https://www.gob.mx/amlo/prensa/presidente-anuncia-inversion-de-10-mil-mdp-para-obras-de-infraestructura-en-cancun-y-tulum","claim":"AMLO announced roughly 10 billion pesos for four Cancun/Tulum works and said the package, together with the Tren Maya-related works, would total about 70 billion pesos, with airport and bridge timelines set for 2023.","locator":"headline and first paragraphs of the press release","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong for the announced commitment and timeline, weaker because it is a plan rather than proof of delivery.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Within the target year and directly tied to 2022 capital allocation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable as an announced executive priority; execution and on-time completion need separate evidence.","contrary_evidence":["Announcements alone do not establish on-budget or on-time completion."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.10"]}
- Major strategic reform setback in energy markets.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexican president's contentious electricity overhaul defeated in Congress","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-17","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/mexican-lawmakers-to-vote-on-presidents-contentious-electricity-overhaul-2804968","claim":"Reuters reported that AMLO's plan to increase state control of power generation was defeated in parliament after opposition parties said it would hurt investment and breach international obligations.","locator":"opening paragraph and vote-result summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a concrete legislative outcome is strong evidence for the failure of this flagship initiative.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and central to the administration's energy program.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: this was AMLO's own flagship reform, though passage depended on Congress and outside constraints.","contrary_evidence":["Defeat reflects legislative limits as well as potential weaknesses in coalition management and persuasion."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
- Inflation crisis response through large subsidies.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico anti-inflation subsidies come with $28 billion price tag","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/mexico-antiinflation-subsidies-come-with-28-billion-price-tag-2860789","claim":"Reuters reported that Mexico spent about 575 billion pesos on anti-inflation subsidies in 2022, mostly gasoline and energy support, and officials said inflation would have been 2.6 percentage points higher without them.","locator":"Reuters report on the subsidy package and official estimate of the inflation effect","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong for the spending scale and official explanation; the effect estimate is official and should be treated cautiously.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 crisis management.","ruler_attribution":"Partly attributable to AMLO's administration because the measures were deliberate policy, but the underlying inflation shock was externally driven and Banxico was independent on interest rates.","contrary_evidence":["The package was expensive and relied heavily on untargeted fuel support, which reduces policy efficiency."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}
- Independent macro assessment of recovery, inflation, and fiscal response.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"El Directorio Ejecutivo del FMI concluye la Consulta del Artículo IV con México correspondiente a 2022","publisher":"Fondo Monetario Internacional","publication_date":"2022-11-04","url":"https://www.imf.org/es/news/articles/2022/11/04/pr22373-imf-executive-board-concludes-2022-article-iv-consultation-with-mexico","claim":"The IMF said Mexico's recovery was gradual, inflation became entrenched, the government kept a broadly neutral fiscal stance in 2022, and largely untargeted subsidies helped support real incomes.","locator":"press-release summary and fiscal-policy discussion","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative external assessment with direct 2022 macro-policy analysis; attribution remains partial because shocks and central-bank actions also matter.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about the target-year macro response.","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the fiscal stance and subsidy package are attributable to the administration, but inflation, growth, and Banxico policy were shaped by external shocks and an independent central bank.","contrary_evidence":["The same IMF assessment highlights entrenched inflation, weaker growth prospects, and persistent structural problems."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I considered roughly 40 documents across official Mexican sources, IMF, OECD, World Bank, CONEVAL, UNICEF, Reuters, and related secondary coverage.
- Kept the strongest non-duplicative items that trace the 2022 program-to-action-to-outcome chain: social transfers, scholarships, rural support, health institutional rollout, wage policy, inflation response, energy reform failure, and broader macro assessments.
- Rejected or downweighted duplicates where multiple mirrors or reposts repeated the same AMLO speech, budget claim, or press release without new material facts.
- Rejected generic context-only material that did not add ruler-specific effectiveness evidence, including broad corruption or freedom indicators, unless the source also tied them to a concrete AMLO program choice or implementation failure.
- Dropped out-of-period follow-ups unless they were clearly retrospective summaries of 2022 outcomes; those were used only when they added independent confirmation of 2022 effects.
- Some direct `gob.mx` pages were blocked on open and had to be handled through search snippets or mirrored official URLs; I kept the version that preserved the clearest locator and avoided duplicate citation of the same statement.

**Remaining Gaps**
- The biggest unresolved question is causal attribution: how much of the 2022 poverty and income improvement came from AMLO-backed policies versus U.S. labor demand, remittances, post-pandemic rebound, and other external conditions.
- There is still limited independent, audit-level evidence on whether flagship infrastructure projects stayed on time and on budget in 2022, especially Tren Maya, AIFA-related works, and aduanas modernization.
- I did not find strong independent evidence that austerity improved state efficiency rather than simply reallocating spending.
- Implementation quality for the social-program registry and targeting remains only partially evidenced; OECD and CONEVAL flag fragmentation and incomplete coverage, but I did not find a cleaner 2022 operational audit.
- If you want a tighter 8B judgment later, more search on project audits, federal procurement, and implementation reports would help.
